<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!--
      Every shipped package multi-targets netstandard2.1;net8.0;net10.0. Without this, each leg gets
      the SDK's default C# version for its TFM - netstandard2.1 would compile as C# 8.0 while net8.0
      gets C# 12 and net10.0 gets C# 14, so shared source using anything newer than C# 8 fails to
      build on the netstandard2.1 leg only.

      Raising this unlocks syntax, not runtime support. Features needing BCL types that
      netstandard2.1 lacks (IsExternalInit for records and init accessors, RequiredMemberAttribute
      for required members, InlineArray/CollectionBuilder for some collection expression targets)
      still fail, as a missing-predefined-type error. Polyfill them internally behind
      #if !NET5_0_OR_GREATER, as PdfPinata/!internal/ and
      PinataLayout.DocumentObjectModel/CompileFixes/ already do. See "Target frameworks" in the
      README for why netstandard2.1 is a target at all.
    -->
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>

    <!--
      CS8073 - "the result of the expression is always false since a value of type T is never equal
      to null of type T?" - is the only thing between a mis-edited struct comparison and a silently
      always-false condition. Comparing a struct that defines operator == against null compiles
      fine, lifts to Nullable<T>, and is never true.

      This is not hypothetical here. Migrating the DOM's nullable wrapper structs turned
      style.IsNull into style == null on four NEnum fields. Two stopped compiling. The other two
      compiled, were always false, and only CS8073 said so. Two more sites in LeftPosition and
      TopPosition would have gone the other way, to an always-true check, for the same reason.

      The tree is clean of it, so this costs nothing today and makes the next such edit fail loudly.
    -->
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);CS8073</WarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
